NNAAMMEE
     xxoo — emit formatted output based on format string and arguments

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     xxoo [--ooppttiioonnss] [_a_r_g_u_m_e_n_t_._._.]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The xxoo utility allows command line access to the functionality of the
     lliibbxxoo library.  Using xxoo, shell scripts can emit _X_M_L, _J_S_O_N, or _H_T_M_L using
     the same commands that emit text output.

     ----cclloossee _p_a_t_h
             Close tags for the given path

     --CC | ----ccoonnttiinnuuaattiioonn
             Indicates this output is a continuation of the previous output
             data and should appear on the same line.  This is allows HTML
             output to be constructed correctly.

     ----ddeepptthh _n_u_m
             Set the depth for pretty printing

     ----hheellpp  Display help text

     --HH | ----hhttmmll
             Generate HTML output

     --JJ | ----jjssoonn
             Generate JSON output

     ----lleeaaddiinngg--xxppaatthh _p_a_t_h
             Add a prefix to generated XPaths (HTML)

     ----nnoott--ffiirrsstt
             Indicate that this content is not the first in a series of sib‐
             ling objects, which is vital information for "JSON" output, which
             requires a comma between such objects.

     ----ooppeenn _p_a_t_h
             Open tags for the given path

     --pp | ----pprreettttyy
             Make 'pretty' output (add indent, newlines)

     ----ssttyyllee _s_t_y_l_e
             Generate given style (xml, json, text, html)

     --TT | ----tteexxtt
             Generate text output (the default style)

     ----ttoopp--wwaarrpp
             Indicates the entire object should be placed inside a top-level
             object wrapper, specifically when generating JSON output.

     ----vveerrssiioonn
             Display version information

     --WW | ----wwaarrnn
             Display warnings in text on stderr

     ----wwaarrnn--xxmmll
             Display warnings in xml on stdout

     ----wwrraapp _p_a_t_h
             Wrap output in a set of containers

     --XX | ----xxmmll
             Generate XML output

     ----xxppaatthh
             Add XPath data to HTML output

     The xxoo utility accepts a format string suitable for xo_emit(3) and a set
     of zero or more arguments used to supply data for that string.

     In addition, xxoo accepts any of the lliibbxxoo options listed in xo_options(7).

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     In this example, xxoo is used to emit the same data encoded in text and
     then in XML by adding the "-p" (pretty) and "-X" (XML output) flags:

             % xo 'The {:product} is {:status}\n' stereo "in route"
             The stereo is in route
             % xo -p -X 'The {:product} is {:status}\n' stereo "in route"
             <product>stereo</product>
             <status>in route</status>

     In this example, the output from a xxoo command is shown in several styles:

             xo "The {k:name} weighs {:weight/%d} pounds.\n" fish 6

             TEXT:
               The fish weighs 6 pounds.
             XML:
               <name>fish</name>
               <weight>6</weight>
             JSON:
               "name": "fish",
               "weight": 6
             HTML:
               <div class="line">
                 <div class="text">The </div>
                 <div class="data" data-tag="name">fish</div>
                 <div class="text"> weighs </div>
                 <div class="data" data-tag="weight">6</div>
                 <div class="text"> pounds.</div>
               </div>

     The ----wwrraapp <<ppaatthh>> option can be used to wrap emitted content in a spe‐
     cific hierarchy.  The path is a set of hierarchical names separated by
     the '/' character.

             xo --wrap top/a/b/c '{:tag}' value

             XML:
               <top>
                 <a>
                   <b>
                     <c>
                       <tag>value</tag>
                     </c>
                   </b>
                 </a>
               </top>
             JSON:
               "top": {
                 "a": {
                   "b": {
                     "c": {
                       "tag": "value"
                     }
                   }
                 }
               }

     The ----ooppeenn <<ppaatthh>> and ----cclloossee <<ppaatthh>> can be used to emit hierarchical in‐
     formation without the matching close and open tag.  This allows a shell
     script to emit open tags, data, and then close tags.  The ----ddeepptthh option
     may be used to set the depth for indentation.  The ----lleeaaddiinngg--xxppaatthh may be
     used to prepend data to the XPath values used for HTML output style.

             #!/bin/sh
             xo --open top/data
             xo --depth 2 '{:tag}' value
             xo --close top/data

             XML:
               <top>
                 <data>
                   <tag>value</tag>
                 </data>
               </top>
             JSON:
               "top": {
                 "data": {
                   "tag": "value"
                 }
               }

